+# Attempts and harness follow-ups
+
+First runner attempt: **38378542755**, source **ae0c2ecc639bb49c723dc1efd6260424a9028a82**. It failed and supplies no complete paired result. Parent preserved the downloaded raw attempt under `evidence/alloc50/attempt-38378542755/`; failures must not be replaced by the later run's success.
+
+- `c256/1-ring/seed.log` reports `invalid GC CPU delta`. A 4096-Put seed can perform no GC, leaving runtime CPU-class deltas stale/zero. The immutable copied bench75 generator remains byte-for-byte unchanged. Only alloc50's invocation changed: runtime metrics flags now attach exclusively to primary `put`, total 60000. Seed, warmup, cases and 2000-Put pprof cohorts still validate exact successes, errors, revisions, terms and process CPU but do not invoke GC-share validation. No GC was inserted around primary timing to hide an invalid delta; a failed primary delta still fails.
+- The original slow fixture plans **4096 stream attempts**, not 4096 demonstrated admissions or proof that every frame was transmitted. Before closing the stalled connection, a healthy Range reads `/alloc50/slow`; its `Version` is the actual committed overwrite count, recorded as `slow_committed_puts`. Ring and arena may admit different counts: separate HEADERS TLS records can charge a full eight-slot arena region for one call. Reserved capacity and committed Puts are reported separately.
+- Parent independently investigated the c64 pristine correctness gate and changed only test fixtures to use production's 100ms tick for allocation tests. The runner overlays exactly `internal/server/server_test.go` and `allocation_path_test.go` from the experiment archive onto the private base archive. The original server fixture, fixture diff and added allocation test are preserved; the actual source manifest includes these test-only overlays. No candidate production code enters the pristine base binary.
+- `TestAllocationPath` changes global profile sampling, so ordinary gates now include only `Allocation(ValueLifetimes|Workspace.*|Shutdown.*)` plus the existing selected correctness cases. After all gates, Path runs alone in a fresh test-binary process for pristine base and experiment base/ring/arena. The matching test binaries/hashes, per-mode logs and before/after profiles are preserved separately under `tests/*-census` and `symbols/*-census.test.gz`.
+
+Local cases follow-up had an initial **lint failure** (`unparam`: attempted-count parameter always 4096); that failure was not claimed as a pass. The helper now uses the same `slowAttempts` constant as the sender/report. The successful follow-up's exact command stdout and exit codes are in `evidence/local-parent/harness-followup.log`; gofumpt, cases short tests, vet and lint each exited zero under the parent's exclusive Go slot. No benchmark or local race run occurred. Parent owns subsequent production/fixture Go runs.
+
+## Second attempt and asynchronous fixture repair
+
+Second run **38381281559**, frozen source **191e12c**, completed all **30 primary timing windows**: each reports 60000 successes, no errors and a valid GC-share metric. These raw timing rows remain usable with their exact-source/workload limitations, but the workflow is **not** a complete diagnostics pass. Parent preserved it under `evidence/alloc50/attempt-38381281559/`.
+
+`cases-ring` at 256 clients and `cases-arena` at 64 failed on the synchronous raw sender's 10-second socket-write deadline, **before healthy traffic began**. Those failures do not prove cross-connection liveness failure. Ring64's completed case recorded 4096 full sends, 256 committed slow Puts, 256 pinned slots, 3840 quota refusals, stable managed bytes and recovery to zero slots / the 8MiB reserve baseline.
+
+The next fixture clears handshake deadlines, returns after launching exactly one sender, and runs healthy work concurrently. Raw writes have a 20-second deadline. Planned4096, actual attempted streams, fully written HEADERS/DATA and DATA bytes are separate counters. A managed blocked prefix is acceptable only after quota/refusal observed within five seconds, at least one second sustained quota, at least1536 healthy Puts, stable bounded snapshots and a healthy Range proving actual committed slow Puts (no more than complete DATA plus one in-progress frame). Baseline must finish all planned sends.
+
+Before intentionally closing a blocked prefix, the case captures the identical observation endpoint's textual goroutine profile. Failures also attempt a diagnostic dump before cleanup when reachable. Close aborts the **underlying TCP socket**, not TLS close_notify; the sender must join within three seconds. Premature errors/timeouts remain failures; only intentional-close-induced closed-connection errors are accepted. Budget recovery and a post-close healthy Put remain mandatory.
+
+Local sender tests cover complete sends, blocked-prefix close/join, premature deadlines and counter/commit bounds. Cases short tests, vet and lint exited zero in `evidence/local-parent/harness-async.log`; these Go checks preceded the type-preserving underlying-TCP handle review adjustment. No additional Go run was performed by this worker after releasing that slot. Python regressions additionally reject late/missing quota, short hold, premature errors, inconsistent counts, excess commits and missing pre-close dumps. Final source validation and new runtime diagnostics belong to the parent/runner. The Actions lifetime-race job now runs cases sender tests sequentially after production lifetime tests.
+
+Every runner artifact includes this note, immutable checked-out harness files, source/fixture patches and available local command logs. No recommendation or throughput gain follows from fixture compilation, fewer mallocs alone, or these repair descriptions; consider CPU, retention and validated lifetime/isolation outcomes separately.
